body:
Reading the deck's raw top-level `templates:` value from kalide.yaml — the value the library resolution needs before a theme registry exists, since deck.LoadConfig needs a theme registry that comes from the not-yet-resolved library — is defined once and used by every call site that reads the raw value: the reload pipeline (internal/server/reload.go, server.configuredTemplates), the file watcher (internal/watch/watch.go, watch.configuredTemplates) and the CLI's library resolution in each of the four commands that resolve a library before loading the deck — internal/cli/start.go, internal/cli/templates.go, internal/cli/check.go and internal/cli/render.go (each carrying the same `fs.ReadFile(deckFS, deck.ConfigFile)` → `yaml.Unmarshal` into `map[string]any` → `raw["templates"].(string)` read). The two CLI test helpers that load a deck a command wrote — internal/cli/upgrade_test.go's `assertUpgradeDeckLoads` and internal/cli/init_test.go's `assertInitDeckLoads` — read the raw value the same way and consume the one shared implementation. A config that cannot be read, cannot be decoded, or has no `templates:` key yields the empty value that selects the deck-root `templates/` layer.

Two neighbouring reads are deliberately not this helper and keep their own behaviour. internal/scaffold/refresh.go's `scaffold.refreshDeckConfig` reads the value through a `yaml:"templates"` struct field and must keep returning its own read and parse errors — `upgrade: read …` for an unreadable kalide.yaml and `upgrade: parse …` for a malformed one — because those errors are never collapsed to the empty value; refreshDeckConfig is never replaced by the shared read. internal/scaffold/external.go's `externalConfig` struct is the write-side read of the marshalled `title` and `templates` fields `kalide init <path>` writes, not the raw `templates:` read, and is unchanged.

AC:
- the reload pipeline, the file watcher, the CLI's four library-resolving commands and the two CLI test helpers read the raw `templates:` value through one shared implementation, and no inline copy of the read remains;
- a config that cannot be read, cannot be decoded, or has no `templates:` key yields the empty value that selects the deck-root `templates/` layer;
- `scaffold.refreshDeckConfig` returns its read and parse errors for an unreadable or malformed kalide.yaml and is not replaced by the shared read;
- internal/scaffold/external.go's `externalConfig` read is unchanged.
